<%# "Challenge to debate" control on an argument (child) card. Only rendered for a
    signed-in viewer who is NOT the argument's author (guarded by the caller).

    The <dialog> exists BEFORE any Debate does, so its element id is scoped to the
    argument — dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog) — NOT a debate. DebatesController's
    create.turbo_stream.erb closes it remotely with the exact same dom_id.

    Each opposing stance is its own button_to POST /hoojah/:slug/debates (params
    argument_id + challenger_stance) — the model enforces challenger_stance !=
    opponent_stance, and offering only the opposing stances keeps the pick valid by
    construction and works with JS off (plain form POST → the debate show page).

    Locals: argument (the child hoojah being challenged), hujah (the root hoojah),
    stance (the argument author's stance name, for the response-filter sync).

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.8) —
    docs/design-system/components/overlays/Dialog.prompt.md, plus
    CompactHujahCard.prompt.md for the trigger, which the design system calls
    `ChallengeLink` and which "renders below the card, never inside it". The panel was
    already the design system's dialog to the letter — 8px rounding, the large shadow,
    the 40% black backdrop, 448px max width, a hairline header carrying the title and an
    X — so the shell does not move, and neither does the header, which is the same markup
    `users/_profile_edit` kept in Task 4.6. What changed:

    - The trigger and the X and Cancel controls all go through
      `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, ...)`, whose emitted string the trigger was
      already spelling by hand almost exactly. The variant is the bare borderless
      transparent text control: pink for the challenge affordance, grey for the two
      dismissals, which is Dialog.prompt.md's "bare grey Cancel". `text-xs` stays at the
      call site because `:link` deliberately carries no font size — this link is 12px,
      not the 16px it would otherwise inherit, and the helper's contract is that a link
      button inherits its context.
    - The stance rows lose the 1px edge and the rounding around each one, and the gap
      between them. That is the same correction Task 4.7 made to the two analytics
      surfaces: this design system spends `#f3f4f6` on hairlines INSIDE a surface
      (`ui/_divider`) and never as an edge around one, and Card.prompt.md forbids
      rounding outright. They do NOT become `ui/_card`s the way those two did — a card
      nested in a dialog is the second shadow the same rule rejects. What is left is the
      shared hairline between rows, which is also what makes this list and the flag
      dialog's reason list render identically at last: they are one component in the
      design system (`DialogChoiceList`) and were two different shapes in the app.
      Row padding is untouched, so the rows sit exactly where they sat.

    FROZEN: `dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog)`, which `debates/create.turbo_stream.erb`
    closes remotely; `data-response-filter-target` / `data-response-filter-vote` on the
    wrapper, which the response filter matches by string against the copies in
    `_response_filter` and `_child_card`; every `data-*` on the trigger and the dialog;
    the POST to /hoojah/:slug/debates with argument_id + challenger_stance; and every word
    of copy — spec/system/debate_spec.rb clicks "Challenge to debate" and "Argue Agree" by
    name. %>
<% stance_labels = {1 => "Agree", 2 => "Neutral", 3 => "Disagree"} %>
<% opponent_stance = argument.vote %>
<div data-controller="dialog"
     data-response-filter-target="item"
     data-response-filter-vote="<%= stance %>"
     class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-1 pr-2">
  <button type="button" data-action="dialog#open"
          class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "neutral") %> text-xs">
    <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %> Challenge to debate
  </button>

  <dialog id="<%= dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog) %>"
          data-dialog-target="dialog"
          data-action="click->dialog#backdropClose close->dialog#restoreFocus"
          aria-labelledby="dialog-title-challenge-<%= argument.id %>"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-lg p-0 w-full max-w-md backdrop:bg-black/40">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-100">
      <h5 id="dialog-title-challenge-<%= argument.id %>" class="text-lg font-medium m-0">
        Challenge @<%= argument.user.username %> to a debate
      </h5>
      <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close" aria-label="Close"
              class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">
        <%= lucide_icon("x", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-grey mb-3">
        They argued <strong><%= stance_labels[opponent_stance] || "their side" %></strong>.
        Pick the side you'll argue — you move first.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <% ([1, 2, 3] - [opponent_stance]).each_with_index do |cs, i| %>
          <%= render "ui/divider" unless i.zero? %>
          <%= button_to "/hoojah/#{hujah.slug}/debates",
                params: {argument_id: argument.id, challenger_stance: cs},
                class: "w-full text-left px-4 py-3 hover:bg-gray-50 bg-white cursor-pointer" do %>
            Argue <strong><%= stance_labels[cs] %></strong>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="text-right mt-4">
        <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close"
                class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">Cancel</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>
